1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,624
[man 1] We've been waiting for hours.

2
00:00:13,625 --> 00:00:15,790
- [nurse] I'm sorry, sir.
- [man 1] How much longer?

3
00:00:15,791 --> 00:00:17,415
- I haven't been seen yet.
- Please, sir.

4
00:00:17,416 --> 00:00:19,999
- I need you to sit down.
- [man 1] Where's the doctor?

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,165
- We've been waiting!
- We have to prioritize emergency cases.

6
00:00:23,166 --> 00:00:25,957
After they've been dealt with,
you'll be able to see a doctor.

7
00:00:25,958 --> 00:00:27,540
- [man 1] What the hell is this?
- Okay.

8
00:00:27,541 --> 00:00:29,707
I'm sorry, you'll have to wait
a little longer.

9
00:00:29,708 --> 00:00:31,624
You too, ma'am. Please take a seat.

10
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:32,875
[patient 1] Doctor!

11
00:00:33,666 --> 00:00:35,457
- [boy groaning]
- How'd he get hurt?

12
00:00:35,458 --> 00:00:37,415
[mother] He fell riding his bike.

13
00:00:37,416 --> 00:00:39,290
- [sighs] You're scaring my kid.
- [boy crying]

14
00:00:39,291 --> 00:00:42,165
- Could we get a different doctor?
- If you want.

15
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:43,708
But you'll be waiting.

16
00:00:44,166 --> 00:00:45,999
[indistinct shouting]

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,874
- Hey! Your AC's too cold.
- Okay, I'll get you a blanket.

18
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:51,749
- Blood's here.
- I want it wide open.

19
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:53,124
He needs it right away. Quickly!

20
00:00:53,125 --> 00:00:54,874
[woman] Doctor, can you save my boyfriend?

21
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:56,499
- Dr. Chiu?
- I'm busy.

22
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,582
The patient's wife said
she doesn't want him revived.

23
00:00:58,583 --> 00:01:00,374
- [machine beeping]
- [woman] No!

24
00:01:00,375 --> 00:01:02,290
[indistinct shouting]

25
00:01:02,291 --> 00:01:03,832
You have to revive him!

26
00:01:03,833 --> 00:01:05,540
Hold on, nurse. Excuse me, nurse?

27
00:01:05,541 --> 00:01:08,165
- Mom wants to go to the restroom.
- My food's getting cold.

28
00:01:08,166 --> 00:01:10,165
- [man 2] I'm alone.
- [patient 2] Can you re-heat it?

29
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:12,332
- Just a moment, uh...
- No. She can't.

30
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:14,166
That isn't a nurse's job.

31
00:01:14,916 --> 00:01:16,415
[male nurse] Calm down, sir. Please.

32
00:01:16,416 --> 00:01:18,165
- [patient 3 groans]
- You're intoxicated.

33
00:01:18,166 --> 00:01:19,957
- I'm trying to help you!
- [patient 3 groans]

34
00:01:19,958 --> 00:01:21,374
- Hey!
- [male nurse] Dr. He.

35
00:01:21,375 --> 00:01:23,290
[slurring] What do you want? [pants]

36
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:25,249
[patient 3 grunting]

37
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:28,083
- [patient 3 groans] What the hell?
- Tranquilizer.

38
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,582
- [patient 3 groaning]
- [male nurse grunting]

39
00:01:31,583 --> 00:01:32,916
[male nurse] Don't move.

40
00:01:35,208 --> 00:01:37,165
- You stay there.
- Restrain him.

41
00:01:37,166 --> 00:01:38,875
- Don't let him attack anyone else.
- Okay.

42
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:44,833
[PA system chimes]

43
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,207
[nurse over PA system]
<i>Chang Chia and family,</i>

44
00:01:47,208 --> 00:01:48,915
<i>please report to the nursing station.</i>

45
00:01:48,916 --> 00:01:52,500
<i>Chang Chia and family,
please report to the nursing station.</i>

46
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,791
[PA system chimes]

47
00:01:55,791 --> 00:01:57,541
[indistinct chatter]

48
00:02:01,583 --> 00:02:03,583
[opening theme music playing]

49
00:02:30,625 --> 00:02:31,999
MIRACLES OF THE ER

50
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,416
EPISODE 1: THE MISFIT

51
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,999
[vehicles honking distantly]

52
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,415
[woman over radio] <i>Golden Melody Award
winning singer, Wei Sung,</i>

53
00:02:42,416 --> 00:02:44,624
<i>- is about to hold his farewell concert.</i>
- [dial tone]

54
00:02:44,625 --> 00:02:47,207
<i>He'll be joining us later
for an exclusive interview</i>

55
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,790
[automated voice] <i>Call could not--</i>

56
00:02:48,791 --> 00:02:50,749
[woman over radio]
<i>...incredible singing career.</i>

57
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:53,124
<i>Wei Sung rose to fame
during the folk movement,</i>

58
00:02:53,125 --> 00:02:55,290
<i>and he has written many timeless classics</i>

59
00:02:55,291 --> 00:02:57,832
<i>including his breakout hit,
"Melody of Life"...</i>

60
00:02:57,833 --> 00:03:00,665
We should've left earlier.
You're always late.

61
00:03:00,666 --> 00:03:02,915
<i>- ...through the darkest moments.</i>
- Dammit.

62
00:03:02,916 --> 00:03:06,457
<i>- This is Wei Sung's "Melody of Life."</i>
- Why isn't Mr. Chen picking up?

63
00:03:06,458 --> 00:03:08,666
["Melody of Life" plays over radio]

64
00:03:10,541 --> 00:03:12,875
[car honks]

65
00:03:15,208 --> 00:03:17,040
- [Mr. Chen] <i>Hello?</i>
- Mr. Chen.

66
00:03:17,041 --> 00:03:19,124
- [Mr. Chen] <i>Can you hear me?</i>
- Yeah, I can hear you.

67
00:03:19,125 --> 00:03:20,499
Is the venue's lighting ready?

68
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,915
Uh, not yet.

69
00:03:21,916 --> 00:03:24,582
But we're handling it right now.
I'm sorry, sir.

70
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:26,291
[metal clanging]

71
00:03:26,875 --> 00:03:29,540
Hey, in there. Have you seen the time?
Lights should be up by now.

72
00:03:29,541 --> 00:03:31,665
[crane operator] Pavement
can't hold the weight.

73
00:03:31,666 --> 00:03:33,791
- [Mr. Chen] Pavement's fine.
- Lift her up.

74
00:03:34,708 --> 00:03:36,290
Yeah, yeah, got it.

75
00:03:36,291 --> 00:03:38,457
[Mr. Chen] Now, we need
to get those boxes unloaded.

76
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:40,249
"MELODY OF LIFE" WEI SUNG
FAREWELL CONCERT

77
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:43,166
- Okay, keep going. Higher.
- [crane beeping]

78
00:03:46,583 --> 00:03:48,958
Bit more, more. Okay.

79
00:03:55,541 --> 00:03:57,165
[clanging]

80
00:03:57,166 --> 00:03:59,708
[ominous music playing]

81
00:04:00,291 --> 00:04:03,665
- [worker and crane operator grunting]
- [bystanders screaming]

82
00:04:03,666 --> 00:04:06,499
[crane operator] Fuck!
I told you it wouldn't hold.

83
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,708
- [worker exclaiming]
- [metal screeching]

84
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:12,082
[shouting]

85
00:04:12,083 --> 00:04:13,999
[bystanders screaming]

86
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,082
- [light shatters]
- [indistinct shouting]

87
00:04:16,083 --> 00:04:18,374
We need assistance here right away.

88
00:04:18,375 --> 00:04:19,957
[worker screaming]

89
00:04:19,958 --> 00:04:22,082
[Mr. Chen] Call them over to help.

90
00:04:22,083 --> 00:04:25,582
- Call 119. We need a rescue team.
- [worker exclaiming]

91
00:04:25,583 --> 00:04:29,415
[worker sobbing, gasping]

92
00:04:29,416 --> 00:04:31,500
[exclaiming]

93
00:04:35,416 --> 00:04:37,707
- [screaming]
- [bystanders shouting]

94
00:04:37,708 --> 00:04:39,749
- [flesh squelches]
- [all screaming]

95
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,332
[siren wailing]

96
00:04:41,333 --> 00:04:43,540
[dispatcher over radio] <i>Unit 92, Unit 92.</i>

97
00:04:43,541 --> 00:04:48,374
<i>Be advised, the fall at Folk Song Square
is being handled by another unit on-site.</i>

98
00:04:48,375 --> 00:04:52,790
<i>Divert immediately to the intersection
at Zhongping and Zhongxiao Road.</i>

99
00:04:52,791 --> 00:04:55,790
<i>There's been a multi-vehicle collision.
Injuries reported.</i>

100
00:04:55,791 --> 00:04:58,500
[EMT] Roger that. We're heading there now.

101
00:05:02,666 --> 00:05:04,958
[vehicles honking]

102
00:05:10,416 --> 00:05:11,790
[man 1 panting]

103
00:05:11,791 --> 00:05:14,665
[man 2] What the hell are you doing?
You hit my car!

104
00:05:14,666 --> 00:05:16,957
[man 3] Hey, hey!
Can I get some help here?

105
00:05:16,958 --> 00:05:18,165
He's bleeding pretty bad.

106
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:20,541
[man 1] Dad? Dad, wake up.

107
00:05:21,458 --> 00:05:23,250
[man 1 pants]

108
00:05:23,916 --> 00:05:26,374
Hello, 119? Yeah.

109
00:05:26,375 --> 00:05:28,832
My dad's unconscious.
I need an ambulance here.

110
00:05:28,833 --> 00:05:30,791
[siren wailing]

111
00:05:31,416 --> 00:05:33,332
- [EMT] Oh, dammit!
- [car honks]

112
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:36,540
- Make way! Hey, there's an ambulance!
- [EMT] Come on.

113
00:05:36,541 --> 00:05:39,040
- Come on, what are you doing?
- [vehicles honking]

114
00:05:39,041 --> 00:05:41,500
[loud music playing on car stereo]

115
00:05:44,083 --> 00:05:46,457
There's an ambulance behind you. Make way.

116
00:05:46,458 --> 00:05:47,666
Thank you.

117
00:05:51,208 --> 00:05:53,040
Drive to your left, please.

118
00:05:53,041 --> 00:05:54,624
[siren continues wailing]

119
00:05:54,625 --> 00:05:57,166
Miss, could you drive
to the right, please?

120
00:05:58,041 --> 00:05:59,708
Uh, to the left, please.

121
00:06:00,208 --> 00:06:01,500
To the right.

122
00:06:03,041 --> 00:06:04,915
Could you drive to the right, please?

123
00:06:04,916 --> 00:06:06,208
Uh, to the left, please.

124
00:06:06,958 --> 00:06:09,166
[car horns honking]

125
00:06:10,458 --> 00:06:12,207
Drive to the right, thank you!

126
00:06:12,208 --> 00:06:13,916
To the left, please.

127
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,333
[siren continues wailing]

128
00:06:26,375 --> 00:06:29,165
- [man 1] Hey, I need help over here.
- [EMT] Who's been injured?

129
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:31,875
- [man 1] It's my dad.
- [EMT] Sir? Can you hear me?

130
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:38,625
[motorcyclist exclaims]

131
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:41,832
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

132
00:06:41,833 --> 00:06:43,375
[telephone ringing]

133
00:06:46,458 --> 00:06:47,791
[knocks on door]

134
00:06:48,375 --> 00:06:50,125
Reporting in? Here.

135
00:06:53,083 --> 00:06:54,500
[man sighs]

136
00:06:55,208 --> 00:06:58,250
Chiang Tung-yen,
Yang-Da first honor graduate.

137
00:06:58,875 --> 00:07:00,624
Tang Hsi, second honor.

138
00:07:00,625 --> 00:07:03,374
And you both chose
Emergency Medicine. Wow. [chuckles]

139
00:07:03,375 --> 00:07:05,208
We're lucky to have such talent.

140
00:07:05,875 --> 00:07:08,750
I am Deputy Director of the department,
Cheng Shao-ching.

141
00:07:09,583 --> 00:07:11,666
On behalf of everyone, welcome.

142
00:07:14,458 --> 00:07:16,749
Well, I hope you can learn a lot here

143
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:19,540
and help strengthen
this department in the future.

144
00:07:19,541 --> 00:07:24,040
Dr. Cheng, I read the guidelines
you published on external trauma wounds.

145
00:07:24,041 --> 00:07:26,291
It's the reason I chose to come here.

146
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,457
Oh, well. Actually, I've been meaning
to write a new guideline paper.

147
00:07:30,458 --> 00:07:33,790
You could join my team in future,
if you're interested.

148
00:07:33,791 --> 00:07:34,915
Oh, really?

149
00:07:34,916 --> 00:07:36,250
Thanks, Dr. Cheng.

150
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,332
[chuckles] Hmm.

151
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:43,333
Aside from you two, another first-year
resident should be reporting today.

152
00:07:44,416 --> 00:07:45,500
Huh.

153
00:07:45,958 --> 00:07:47,583
Handpicked by Dr. Chou.

154
00:07:48,166 --> 00:07:51,375
Guess punctuality
isn't their strong suit. [chuckles]

155
00:07:52,791 --> 00:07:54,957
[panting]

156
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:56,374
[Shao-ching gulps]

157
00:07:56,375 --> 00:07:57,499
[pants]

158
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:59,332
Lin Geng-ming, reporting!

159
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:01,458
[exciting music playing]

160
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:05,208
[chuckles]

161
00:08:07,416 --> 00:08:09,958
[exhales, chuckles]

162
00:08:15,583 --> 00:08:18,832
I guess we're colleagues now.
I'm Lin Geng-ming.

163
00:08:18,833 --> 00:08:21,708
What's your name? Uh, Chiang Tung-yen.

164
00:08:22,208 --> 00:08:23,582
And you are...

165
00:08:23,583 --> 00:08:24,874
Oh, I'm not important.

166
00:08:24,875 --> 00:08:27,332
What matters is
if you can actually treat patients.

167
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:29,250
Just don't slow us down.

168
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:33,457
Tang Hsi. [chuckles]

169
00:08:33,458 --> 00:08:34,541
I saw it.

170
00:08:35,083 --> 00:08:37,499
- [indistinct chatter]
- Right here is the nursing station.

171
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,541
This will be your home base.

172
00:08:41,208 --> 00:08:42,749
[patient moaning in pain]

173
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:44,790
- [woman] And then he fell.
- He fell?

174
00:08:44,791 --> 00:08:47,124
- [woman] Yeah.
- [man] Why isn't he seen by a doctor?

175
00:08:47,125 --> 00:08:49,207
- [woman] I don't know.
- Chiu. Chiu, come here.

176
00:08:49,208 --> 00:08:51,832
- I have a patient.
- [Shao-ching] It'll only take a minute.

177
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:53,749
I'd like you to meet the new R1s.

178
00:08:53,750 --> 00:08:55,665
This is Dr. Chiu.

179
00:08:55,666 --> 00:08:57,040
He'll take you from here.

180
00:08:57,041 --> 00:08:59,082
Thanks, Doctor. I'll leave you to it.

181
00:08:59,083 --> 00:09:01,790
- Dr. Chiu.
- [loudly] Hi, Dr. Chiu. I'm Lin Geng-ming.

182
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,749
Yeah, you don't need to talk so loud.

183
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:06,874
- I'm really busy--
- [nurse over PA system] <i>Emergency 333!</i>

184
00:09:06,875 --> 00:09:08,749
<i>Emergency 333!</i>

185
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:10,624
[tense music playing]

186
00:09:10,625 --> 00:09:12,125
[PA system chimes]

187
00:09:14,416 --> 00:09:16,332
- Excuse me, coming through.
- Make way.

188
00:09:16,333 --> 00:09:18,040
Clear the way, please!

189
00:09:18,041 --> 00:09:19,749
- Hey, over here.
- [Chih-cheng] What you got?

190
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:21,832
[EMT 1] Severe bleeding,
trauma wound left foot.

191
00:09:21,833 --> 00:09:24,499
- BP is 90 over 50, heart rate 130.
- [patient groaning]

192
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,416
[tense music playing]

193
00:09:29,708 --> 00:09:31,790
- Hey, stop blocking the way!
- [Geng-ming panting]

194
00:09:31,791 --> 00:09:33,332
Bring him to Resus 2.

195
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:35,332
Run two IVs. A liter of saline.

196
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:37,374
Cross-match blood and call Orthopedics.

197
00:09:37,375 --> 00:09:39,124
You two, help out back.

198
00:09:39,125 --> 00:09:40,499
[rapid footsteps departing]

199
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:41,665
What do we have here?

200
00:09:41,666 --> 00:09:43,749
[EMT 2] 63-year-old, MBA,
severe head trauma.

201
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,458
- Altered consciousness.
- Careful!

202
00:09:46,625 --> 00:09:47,790
Okay, and this one?

203
00:09:47,791 --> 00:09:50,624
[EMT 3] 62-year-old male,
unconscious, no external injuries.

204
00:09:50,625 --> 00:09:52,000
[all] One, two, three!

205
00:09:53,416 --> 00:09:56,457
R1s, I don't have time
to ease you into this.

206
00:09:56,458 --> 00:09:57,957
Dr. Huang, you lead Tung-yen.

207
00:09:57,958 --> 00:09:59,665
Tang Hsi, you're with Dr. Chiu.

208
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:01,916
- You, follow me. Quick.
- [male nurse] Come on!

209
00:10:04,333 --> 00:10:05,333
Hurry!

210
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:11,915
- [Yu-hua] What are his vitals?
- Heart rate 112, BP 82 over 45.

211
00:10:11,916 --> 00:10:13,541
- It keeps dropping.
- [machine beeping]

212
00:10:16,458 --> 00:10:17,957
Please save my dad.

213
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:19,457
Family can't be in here.

214
00:10:19,458 --> 00:10:21,874
- Doctor, please--
- Sorry, I need you to step out.

215
00:10:21,875 --> 00:10:23,582
- Prepare for intubation.
- [nurse] Yes, Doctor.

216
00:10:23,583 --> 00:10:25,665
- Hsiu-ju, Esmeron, 50.
- Okay.

217
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:27,291
R1, you're up.

218
00:10:27,875 --> 00:10:29,041
Intubate.

219
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:32,833
[Hsiu-ju] Esmeron, 50 milligrams, done.

220
00:10:33,416 --> 00:10:34,500
[nurse] Ready for intubation.

221
00:10:36,958 --> 00:10:38,832
- CO2 is at 100.
- [Yu-hua] Okay.

222
00:10:38,833 --> 00:10:40,500
Do it now, hurry.

223
00:10:41,583 --> 00:10:42,625
Here.

224
00:10:45,708 --> 00:10:48,791
Vocal cords above, esophagus below. Okay.

225
00:10:49,666 --> 00:10:51,791
[breathing heavily, exhales deeply]

226
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:55,166
- [breathing heavily]
- [machine beeping]

227
00:10:57,416 --> 00:10:58,833
- Tube.
- [nurse] Here.

228
00:11:05,958 --> 00:11:07,125
- Okay?
- Okay.

229
00:11:09,833 --> 00:11:10,958
[sighs in relief]

230
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,958
- [groans]
- [grunts]

231
00:11:13,583 --> 00:11:15,000
[panting]

232
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,290
The tube's in the esophagus.
Get it out now!

233
00:11:17,291 --> 00:11:19,249
Suction. Hurry!

234
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,665
[nurses sigh]

235
00:11:20,666 --> 00:11:22,583
[machine beeping]

236
00:11:26,458 --> 00:11:27,833
[liquid draining]

237
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:29,915
It's all clear.

238
00:11:29,916 --> 00:11:31,208
[machine beeping rapidly]

239
00:11:31,791 --> 00:11:33,082
There's no pulse.

240
00:11:33,083 --> 00:11:34,291
CPR!

241
00:11:37,791 --> 00:11:39,208
[Yu-hua panting]

242
00:11:39,791 --> 00:11:42,250
Why are you standing there?
Do another intubation!

243
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,582
You're using the wrong hand.
Can you do one or not?

244
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:50,791
Sorry, sorry.

245
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,332
- Hsiu-ju, swap.
- Okay.

246
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:54,624
Three, two, one.

247
00:11:54,625 --> 00:11:55,790
[Hsiu-ju panting]

248
00:11:55,791 --> 00:11:57,083
[Yu-hua] Out of the way!

249
00:11:57,666 --> 00:11:59,082
Don't touch him.

250
00:11:59,083 --> 00:12:01,333
- [machine continues beeping]
- [Hsiu-ju panting]

251
00:12:01,791 --> 00:12:03,208
- Tube now.
- [nurse] Here.

252
00:12:04,208 --> 00:12:05,541
Hold compressions.

253
00:12:08,375 --> 00:12:09,250
It's in.

254
00:12:13,375 --> 00:12:14,790
[Geng-ming breathing heavily]

255
00:12:14,791 --> 00:12:16,874
[machine beeping stabilizes]

256
00:12:16,875 --> 00:12:18,166
[Hsiu-ju] Pulse is back.

257
00:12:18,666 --> 00:12:19,833
[Yu-hua] Okay.

258
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,999
[woman on phone] <i>Ms. Chang,
the minister is two minutes away.</i>

259
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,083
[Chia-hsin] <i>Okay.</i>

260
00:12:31,583 --> 00:12:32,916
This way, please.

261
00:12:34,708 --> 00:12:37,083
- Director Chang and the others are here.
- [Minister] Thank you.

262
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,665
[doctor] Director Chang, the minister.

263
00:12:39,666 --> 00:12:40,999
- Hello, sir.
- Ah!

264
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,082
- Minister, good to see you.
- Director Chang.

265
00:12:43,083 --> 00:12:45,374
And thanks for taking time
out of your busy schedule.

266
00:12:45,375 --> 00:12:47,707
Enough with the formalities.
We're old classmates.

267
00:12:47,708 --> 00:12:49,499
- Now, where's the star of the show?
- Oh!

268
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:51,665
Of course, let me introduce you.

269
00:12:51,666 --> 00:12:52,791
Uh...

270
00:12:53,375 --> 00:12:54,874
[whispers] He hasn't arrived yet.

271
00:12:54,875 --> 00:12:56,583
[dramatic music playing]

272
00:13:02,625 --> 00:13:03,957
Uh... Um...

273
00:13:03,958 --> 00:13:06,458
- He's here. Dr. Chou is here.
- [rapid footsteps approaching]

274
00:13:07,208 --> 00:13:08,665
Hi. Sorry I'm late.

275
00:13:08,666 --> 00:13:09,915
At the end of my shift,

276
00:13:09,916 --> 00:13:12,249
a patient came in
with massive hemorrhaging.

277
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:14,375
- I had to get him into the OR.
- Hmm.

278
00:13:15,666 --> 00:13:18,415
Minister, I'd like for you to meet

279
00:13:18,416 --> 00:13:21,458
Deputy Director of the ER,
Dr. Chou Cheng-chun.

280
00:13:22,125 --> 00:13:25,457
He's also the one in charge
of the anti-violence device.

281
00:13:25,458 --> 00:13:26,500
[Minister] Dr. Chou.

282
00:13:27,041 --> 00:13:28,290
I've heard a lot about you.

283
00:13:28,291 --> 00:13:30,708
You always put your patients first,
I admire that.

284
00:13:31,333 --> 00:13:33,874
Okay, the press conference
is about to start.

285
00:13:33,875 --> 00:13:36,125
- Great.
- [Chia-hsin] Please take a seat.

286
00:13:41,958 --> 00:13:43,249
[Cheng-chun sighs]

287
00:13:43,250 --> 00:13:45,791
I couldn't get in contact with you.
I was worried.

288
00:13:46,291 --> 00:13:47,541
Can I go now?

289
00:13:48,416 --> 00:13:50,124
Come on, you only just got here.

290
00:13:50,125 --> 00:13:53,540
Thirty minutes. I promise
I'll let you go in 30 minutes.

291
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:54,958
[Cheng-chun sighs]

292
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:57,708
LIN GENG-MING

293
00:13:58,208 --> 00:14:00,791
[scoffs] "Are you okay?"

294
00:14:01,291 --> 00:14:02,291
Are you?

295
00:14:03,458 --> 00:14:04,666
I'm okay.

296
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:06,375
[chuckles]

297
00:14:07,375 --> 00:14:09,333
Take a look at the minor cases.

298
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,833
Okay. Thanks, Dr. Cheng.

299
00:14:17,875 --> 00:14:19,125
[nurse] Dr. Cheng.

300
00:14:19,666 --> 00:14:22,249
The patient who fell off the bed earlier,
Li Wen-hsiung,

301
00:14:22,250 --> 00:14:24,374
is complaining about severe chest pain.

302
00:14:24,375 --> 00:14:26,249
Did you administer painkillers?

303
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:29,166
Yes, but his BP's a bit low
and he's short of breath.

304
00:14:30,041 --> 00:14:31,458
[Shao-ching sighs]

305
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:34,832
[patient groaning]

306
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:36,207
- [man] Doctor.
- [woman] Doctor.

307
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:38,540
How are you feeling? Where does it hurt?

308
00:14:38,541 --> 00:14:40,540
Why is his condition getting worse?

309
00:14:40,541 --> 00:14:42,540
Is it because he fell off
the bed just now?

310
00:14:42,541 --> 00:14:44,415
- Does he have internal bleeding?
- Here.

311
00:14:44,416 --> 00:14:46,083
All right, inhale.

312
00:14:46,958 --> 00:14:48,083
Exhale.

313
00:14:49,208 --> 00:14:50,790
- Inhale.
- [Wen-hsiung inhales]

314
00:14:50,791 --> 00:14:53,416
- Exhale.
- [Wen-hsiung exhales hoarsely]

315
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,457
We'll start with a painkiller injection
to make him comfortable.

316
00:14:56,458 --> 00:14:58,790
- We'll arrange for some more tests.
- [Wen-hsiung groaning]

317
00:14:58,791 --> 00:15:02,333
Give him half a dose of morphine
and keep him under observation.

318
00:15:02,916 --> 00:15:04,041
Yes, Doctor.

319
00:15:04,625 --> 00:15:06,000
Uh, hey!

320
00:15:06,916 --> 00:15:08,750
[Wen-hsiung groaning softly]

321
00:15:09,833 --> 00:15:11,791
Uh... Nurse.

322
00:15:12,375 --> 00:15:14,375
What's my dad's condition now?

323
00:15:15,916 --> 00:15:18,332
- We need to keep observing him.
- [Wen-hsiung groaning]

324
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:19,541
So you don't know.

325
00:15:21,458 --> 00:15:24,499
Hello, Dr. Hsieh, it's Cheng Shao-ching.

326
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,582
Uh, can I ask you
about a patient's condition?

327
00:15:27,583 --> 00:15:31,332
He says he has chest pains
and he isn't breathing very well...

328
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:34,624
Hey, Su-ching, Dr. Cheng's patient
isn't doing well.

329
00:15:34,625 --> 00:15:38,290
Dr. Cheng only prescribed painkillers,
and now he's on the phone.

330
00:15:38,291 --> 00:15:40,916
[inhales] He probably wants
a second opinion.

331
00:15:41,541 --> 00:15:44,499
Don't worry. Once he finds help,
he'll give you instruction.

332
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,833
- Just get back to work.
- [sighs]

333
00:15:47,666 --> 00:15:49,457
Hey! What's going on?

334
00:15:49,458 --> 00:15:52,957
We've been waiting here for two hours.
Why haven't we been admitted yet?

335
00:15:52,958 --> 00:15:55,457
- What exactly are you so busy with, huh?
- [keyboard clacking]

336
00:15:55,458 --> 00:15:57,665
Sorry, there's no beds
available at the moment.

337
00:15:57,666 --> 00:15:59,124
You'll need to wait a little longer.

338
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:01,082
[shouting] Yeah? Well, how much longer?

339
00:16:01,083 --> 00:16:04,707
Excuse me, ma'am. We're here to help you.
When there's a bed, we'll let you know.

340
00:16:04,708 --> 00:16:07,790
I don't need a nurse to help me.
What I need is a doctor!

341
00:16:07,791 --> 00:16:10,249
My father-in-law
is very uncomfortable in there!

342
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:13,250
Perhaps you'd like to transfer
to a different hospital, then.

343
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:16,249
- Also, we're registered nurses.
- [telephone rings]

344
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:17,791
- Hey!
- [Su-ching] Hello. Yang-Da ER.

345
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,999
Hsiang-chun. Let us know what you decide.

346
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,874
- Hey!
- [Su-ching] Quick! Get the bed.

347
00:16:22,875 --> 00:16:24,082
[Hsiang-chun] Okay.

348
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:26,791
- Make way, please! Coming through.
- Excuse us.

349
00:16:27,541 --> 00:16:28,999
Bed coming through.

350
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,249
[Hsiang-chun] Bed coming through!
Coming through. Make way.

351
00:16:32,250 --> 00:16:35,000
- [Yu-hua] Excuse us. Bed coming!
- Okay, keep driving.

352
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,666
- They're right behind us.
- [whistle blows]

353
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:39,832
- [whistle blows]
- [man] Come on!

354
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:41,000
Over here.

355
00:16:42,541 --> 00:16:45,290
- Careful.
- Guys, get down. Doctor's coming up.

356
00:16:45,291 --> 00:16:47,415
- [EMT 1] Hang in there.
- [Yu-hua] Let's go up.

357
00:16:47,416 --> 00:16:49,790
- [guard] Let them through.
- [EMT 1] We're at the hospital.

358
00:16:49,791 --> 00:16:51,957
- Help is on its way.
- What are we looking at?

359
00:16:51,958 --> 00:16:54,124
[EMT 1] Patient is suffering
from massive blood loss.

360
00:16:54,125 --> 00:16:56,207
- Statue's still in there.
- How did this happen?

361
00:16:56,208 --> 00:16:59,624
[EMT 1] He fell working on a high-rise.
Torch pierced his abdomen.

362
00:16:59,625 --> 00:17:02,458
BP 70 over 40, heart rate 142.

363
00:17:04,625 --> 00:17:06,541
[patient moaning in pain]

364
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:09,958
- Hsiang-chun, inform the OR.
- Okay.

365
00:17:11,916 --> 00:17:14,540
[Yu-hua] Sir, you're at the hospital now.
Hang in there, okay?

366
00:17:14,541 --> 00:17:17,458
[guard] Excuse me.
Ambulance is coming through. Make way!

367
00:17:18,125 --> 00:17:21,041
[EMT 1] Help is coming.
Just hang in there a little longer.

368
00:17:24,458 --> 00:17:25,833
[Yu-hua] Right here.

369
00:17:27,166 --> 00:17:28,875
[machine powering up]

370
00:17:31,791 --> 00:17:34,333
[indistinct chatter]

371
00:17:35,916 --> 00:17:37,665
[blade whirring]

372
00:17:37,666 --> 00:17:41,125
Dr. Tang, why is the patient's BP so low?

373
00:17:41,708 --> 00:17:43,332
There's massive internal bleeding.

374
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:45,583
Aside from a blood transfusion,
what can be done?

375
00:17:47,625 --> 00:17:48,916
A REBOA,

376
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,791
to stop the bleeding,
and buy the patient more time.

377
00:17:56,416 --> 00:17:58,291
[Yu-hua] Bring him to the Resus Room.

378
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,499
At Yang-Da Hospital,

379
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:05,874
we're committed to preventing violence
against medical personnel.

380
00:18:05,875 --> 00:18:09,999
In future, we will equip
each and every healthcare worker

381
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,208
with one of these anti-violence devices.

382
00:18:13,791 --> 00:18:16,790
In an emergency,
all it takes is the press of a button

383
00:18:16,791 --> 00:18:19,290
and security will arrive
within 30 seconds.

384
00:18:19,291 --> 00:18:23,082
Our goal is simple, to help
every healthcare worker do their job

385
00:18:23,083 --> 00:18:25,457
and protect their life without hesitation.

386
00:18:25,458 --> 00:18:27,540
[audience applauding]

387
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:30,332
Wait, Doctor.
What exactly is going on with my dad?

388
00:18:30,333 --> 00:18:32,999
Please don't worry.
I've contacted Surgery for consult.

389
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,540
We're dealing with a large number
of patients right now.

390
00:18:35,541 --> 00:18:38,499
- So you'll have to wait a little longer.
- [woman] How much longer?

391
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:39,540
I just checked online

392
00:18:39,541 --> 00:18:42,290
and it says that chest pain
could be due to aortic dissection.

393
00:18:42,291 --> 00:18:43,582
We're racing against time!

394
00:18:43,583 --> 00:18:45,915
Please don't use Google
to make your own diagnosis.

395
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:47,999
- You can trust the doctors here.
- Just a second.

396
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,082
When can they do a proper examination?

397
00:18:50,083 --> 00:18:51,915
Like I said, all doctors are busy.

398
00:18:51,916 --> 00:18:54,874
It says here you're a doctor
and you don't look too busy.

399
00:18:54,875 --> 00:18:56,874
- Keep it down.
- Are you really a doctor?

400
00:18:56,875 --> 00:18:59,457
- Yes, I've written a lot of papers.
- If you can't do your job,

401
00:18:59,458 --> 00:19:02,249
- I want to talk to the director!
- I'm calling security right now.

402
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:04,415
- [phone buzzing]
- [Hsueh-hung] I must also thank

403
00:19:04,416 --> 00:19:07,332
- Chairman Wu from Smart Star Technology...
- [quietly] Hello?

404
00:19:07,333 --> 00:19:09,915
[Hsueh-hung] ...who developed
this anti-violence device.

405
00:19:09,916 --> 00:19:12,582
- [audience applauding]
- All right, I'll come now.

406
00:19:12,583 --> 00:19:15,749
[Hsueh-hung] The Director of Yang-Da's
Department of Emergency Medicine,

407
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:17,583
Dr. Chung Sheng-shan.

408
00:19:19,125 --> 00:19:22,957
And the person in charge of implementing
the device at our hospital,

409
00:19:22,958 --> 00:19:25,000
Dr. Chou Cheng-chun.

410
00:19:29,666 --> 00:19:31,250
[applause fades]

411
00:19:32,166 --> 00:19:33,958
[indistinct whispers]

412
00:19:34,625 --> 00:19:36,749
- [man] You're a disgrace.
- This man is Dr. Cheng.

413
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:39,290
- You stop filming, now.
- Hey, don't go near her!

414
00:19:39,291 --> 00:19:42,040
I'm a doctor. I need this hand!
Let go of me. It hurts.

415
00:19:42,041 --> 00:19:45,583
- Dr. Cheng! The patient is unresponsive.
- [machine beeping rapidly]

416
00:19:46,333 --> 00:19:48,875
Sir? Sir, can you hear me?

417
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:52,082
No pulse. CPR.

418
00:19:52,083 --> 00:19:54,749
Prep for intubation.
Epi, one every three minutes.

419
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:56,875
- Ah, yes, Doctor.
- [machine continues beeping]

420
00:20:00,083 --> 00:20:01,083
[man] What's happening?

421
00:20:04,416 --> 00:20:06,291
- [Tung-yen] Done?
- Yeah, it's done.

422
00:20:10,333 --> 00:20:12,790
- [man] How's my dad?
- [woman] Doctor? Nurse?

423
00:20:12,791 --> 00:20:14,457
[panting] Is he going to be okay?

424
00:20:14,458 --> 00:20:16,290
- [Hsiang-chun] Doctor's handling it.
- Tubes.

425
00:20:16,291 --> 00:20:18,040
- Right here.
- [Hsiang-chun] Don't worry.

426
00:20:18,041 --> 00:20:19,457
Okay.

427
00:20:19,458 --> 00:20:20,791
Pull out.

428
00:20:24,458 --> 00:20:26,416
- Checking.
- [machine continues beeping]

429
00:20:28,583 --> 00:20:29,583
Okay.

430
00:20:33,125 --> 00:20:35,332
- What the hell's happening?
- Please don't act like this.

431
00:20:35,333 --> 00:20:36,999
- [man] I'll sue you.
- What if my dad dies?

432
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,875
[yelling] You want me a piece of me, huh?

433
00:20:41,833 --> 00:20:43,457
I'll treat your dad from here.

434
00:20:43,458 --> 00:20:45,541
Calm down. We'll do everything we can.

435
00:20:46,291 --> 00:20:48,458
[woman panting]

436
00:20:49,458 --> 00:20:51,083
[machine beeping stabilizes]

437
00:20:53,041 --> 00:20:54,165
We got ROSC.

438
00:20:54,166 --> 00:20:56,374
- What's his BP?
- 65 over 30.

439
00:20:56,375 --> 00:20:58,500
- Bring in the echo.
- Yes, Doctor.

440
00:21:10,375 --> 00:21:13,207
Pleural effusion, on the left side.

441
00:21:13,208 --> 00:21:15,332
Likely, it's a hemothorax. Call Surgery.

442
00:21:15,333 --> 00:21:17,749
- Okay.
- [Cheng-chun] Give me a 32F chest tube.

443
00:21:17,750 --> 00:21:20,874
- Is a hemothorax really bad?
- Don't worry, I'm handling it.

444
00:21:20,875 --> 00:21:22,165
[nurse] Surgery? This is ER.

445
00:21:22,166 --> 00:21:24,374
We have a patient
that needs emergency attention.

446
00:21:24,375 --> 00:21:26,832
- [machine beeping rapidly]
- Dr. Chou, asystole.

447
00:21:26,833 --> 00:21:28,624
- Continue CPR.
- Okay.

448
00:21:28,625 --> 00:21:30,250
- You got this?
- Yeah.

449
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:34,625
[Tung-yen panting]

450
00:21:38,375 --> 00:21:39,500
Okay, got it.

451
00:21:40,083 --> 00:21:41,749
Dr. Chou, they need at least 30 minutes.

452
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:44,915
He told us to contact them
when there's vital signs.

453
00:21:44,916 --> 00:21:46,207
It'll be too late.

454
00:21:46,208 --> 00:21:48,457
Thoracotomy. You assist.

455
00:21:48,458 --> 00:21:50,500
[Tung-yen panting]

456
00:21:51,875 --> 00:21:53,707
Bring him to the Resus Room.

457
00:21:53,708 --> 00:21:55,250
- Now?
- [nurse] Yes, Doctor.

458
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:58,125
- Are they gonna operate?
- I don't know.

459
00:22:00,041 --> 00:22:02,374
- [Tung-yen] Excuse us!
- [Hsiang-chun] Coming through!

460
00:22:02,375 --> 00:22:04,999
- Clear the aisle, please.
- Dr. Chou! Are you crazy?

461
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,915
You're an emergency physician,
not a surgeon. Don't be reckless.

462
00:22:07,916 --> 00:22:10,500
He can't wait any longer.
We have to save him.

463
00:22:20,833 --> 00:22:23,999
- [machine beeping faintly]
- There's a pulse. We still can't get a BP.

464
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,457
There's gonna be massive bleeding.

465
00:22:25,458 --> 00:22:26,832
- Be prepared.
- [Tung-yen] Okay.

466
00:22:26,833 --> 00:22:27,958
[Cheng-chun] Scalpel.

467
00:22:48,083 --> 00:22:50,665
[Yu-hua] Remember not to touch
the torch during surgery.

468
00:22:50,666 --> 00:22:52,790
It can trigger massive hemorrhaging.

469
00:22:52,791 --> 00:22:54,957
[Hsi] His BP keeps dropping.

470
00:22:54,958 --> 00:22:57,458
[tense music playing]

471
00:23:05,541 --> 00:23:08,749
INFLATE AN AORTIC BALLOON
TO TEMPORARILY STOP BLEEDING.

472
00:23:08,750 --> 00:23:12,707
[Yu-hua] Dr. Tang, which zone of the aorta
should the catheter be inserted?

473
00:23:12,708 --> 00:23:16,333
[Hsi] From the left subclavian artery
to the celiac artery.

474
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:19,249
[Yu-hua] What are the risks?

475
00:23:19,250 --> 00:23:22,041
[Hsi] Aortic dissection
or vascular rupture.

476
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,166
[Cheng-chun] Kelly.

477
00:23:32,666 --> 00:23:34,874
I'm gonna spread the pleura open now.

478
00:23:34,875 --> 00:23:36,166
[flesh squelching]

479
00:23:36,666 --> 00:23:38,790
- [Cheng-chun grunts]
- [Tung-yen breathes heavily]

480
00:23:38,791 --> 00:23:41,165
- [Cheng-chun] Suction.
- [Tung-yen] Okay.

481
00:23:41,166 --> 00:23:43,915
- [Cheng-chun] Scissors.
- [nurse] Hsiang-chun, more gauze.

482
00:23:43,916 --> 00:23:46,000
[tense music playing]

483
00:23:54,750 --> 00:23:56,500
[suction continues]

484
00:23:58,916 --> 00:24:00,500
[Cheng-chun] Rib spreader.

485
00:24:05,541 --> 00:24:07,666
[metal clanking]

486
00:24:15,041 --> 00:24:17,708
[Hsi] Doctor, would you let me do it?

487
00:24:18,791 --> 00:24:20,458
[male nurse] Catheter's ready.

488
00:24:21,625 --> 00:24:24,707
[Yu-hua] A REBOA is very difficult.
Are you confident?

489
00:24:24,708 --> 00:24:27,124
- [Hsi] I can do it.
- [Yu-hua] Mmm.

490
00:24:27,125 --> 00:24:29,708
[tense music continues]

491
00:24:33,666 --> 00:24:34,791
Gel.

492
00:24:37,333 --> 00:24:39,083
Be careful with the guide wire.

493
00:24:40,250 --> 00:24:41,666
[male nurse] Wire's here.

494
00:24:42,708 --> 00:24:44,458
[gel squelching]

495
00:24:48,416 --> 00:24:49,666
[blood squelching]

496
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:52,583
[Cheng-chun] Push aside the lung lobe.

497
00:24:57,291 --> 00:24:59,375
The position isn't right.

498
00:24:59,958 --> 00:25:01,375
Scissors. Forceps.

499
00:25:10,541 --> 00:25:13,790
I've cut open the pericardium.
Tung-yen, find the source of the bleeding.

500
00:25:13,791 --> 00:25:15,083
[Tung-yen] Okay.

501
00:25:17,083 --> 00:25:19,083
[squelching]

502
00:25:22,333 --> 00:25:23,915
I can't find it.

503
00:25:23,916 --> 00:25:26,500
[Cheng-chun] Take your time.
It's at the back here.

504
00:25:31,041 --> 00:25:33,666
It's an aortic injury. Gauze first.

505
00:25:38,583 --> 00:25:40,208
Vascular clamp.

506
00:25:45,125 --> 00:25:47,416
Continue suction. 3-0 Prolene.

507
00:25:51,750 --> 00:25:53,708
[squelching]

508
00:26:08,708 --> 00:26:10,541
[machine beeping faintly]

509
00:26:12,875 --> 00:26:15,458
[Yu-hua] Position's good. Inject contrast.

510
00:26:27,875 --> 00:26:28,833
Wait.

511
00:26:29,875 --> 00:26:31,833
How much for Zone 1?

512
00:26:32,541 --> 00:26:33,790
[Hsi] 8 cc.

513
00:26:33,791 --> 00:26:36,457
Any more than that
would cause damage to the aorta.

514
00:26:36,458 --> 00:26:37,500
[Yu-hua] Mmm.

515
00:26:42,041 --> 00:26:45,666
Now, examine
the contralateral femoral artery.

516
00:26:49,291 --> 00:26:51,750
[Hsi] We did it. Pulse detected.

517
00:26:53,458 --> 00:26:54,875
Great. BP's back.

518
00:26:56,250 --> 00:26:58,457
[Yu-hua] Okay. Contact Surgery.

519
00:26:58,458 --> 00:27:01,125
- Tell them to take over.
- [male nurse] Yes, Doctor.

520
00:27:11,583 --> 00:27:12,791
[Cheng-chun] Scissors.

521
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,541
[Tung-yen sighs]

522
00:27:21,791 --> 00:27:23,541
[machine beeping rapidly]

523
00:27:25,083 --> 00:27:26,041
Asystole.

524
00:27:27,166 --> 00:27:28,832
[Tung-yen]
The blood vessel's been sutured.

525
00:27:28,833 --> 00:27:30,790
Why's it still in asystole?

526
00:27:30,791 --> 00:27:32,332
[nurse] What should we do?

527
00:27:32,333 --> 00:27:34,041
[machine continues beeping]

528
00:27:46,541 --> 00:27:48,666
[flesh squelching]

529
00:27:58,958 --> 00:28:01,458
[machine beeping stabilizes]

530
00:28:06,208 --> 00:28:08,666
His heart rate's back. [exhales]

531
00:28:09,208 --> 00:28:12,457
[Cheng-chun] Contact Cardiovascular.
Ask them to get the patient to the OR.

532
00:28:12,458 --> 00:28:13,916
Yes, Doctor.

533
00:28:14,416 --> 00:28:15,958
[sighs in relief]

534
00:28:16,458 --> 00:28:19,249
Thank God for Dr. Chou.
Good thing he's here.

535
00:28:19,250 --> 00:28:21,291
[tools clanging]

536
00:28:21,875 --> 00:28:24,957
[Hsiang-chun] This is ER. We have
a patient who underwent a thoracotomy.

537
00:28:24,958 --> 00:28:26,874
He's ready for you now.

538
00:28:26,875 --> 00:28:28,957
- Thank you.
- [Sheng-shan] Take care, Chairman.

539
00:28:28,958 --> 00:28:30,833
- You, too.
- Okay, this way.

540
00:28:32,666 --> 00:28:33,832
[reporter] Director Chang!

541
00:28:33,833 --> 00:28:36,707
Was today's press conference
on the anti-violence device

542
00:28:36,708 --> 00:28:40,749
an attempt to distract from the hospital's
recent string of malpractice cases?

543
00:28:40,750 --> 00:28:42,790
I'm sorry, Director Chang
has another appointment.

544
00:28:42,791 --> 00:28:44,915
He won't be accepting interviews today.

545
00:28:44,916 --> 00:28:47,582
- Okay? Thank you.
- It's all right. I can answer.

546
00:28:47,583 --> 00:28:49,165
Thank you, everyone.

547
00:28:49,166 --> 00:28:53,082
With medical disputes,
regardless of the legal outcome,

548
00:28:53,083 --> 00:28:54,957
no one comes out a winner.

549
00:28:54,958 --> 00:28:58,290
I would first like to offer
my deepest sympathy

550
00:28:58,291 --> 00:29:00,083
to everyone involved.

551
00:29:04,500 --> 00:29:08,957
We have consistently strived
to reflect and review our practices.

552
00:29:08,958 --> 00:29:11,707
To make fundamental changes and reform.

553
00:29:11,708 --> 00:29:13,707
- [phone buzzing]
- Be it medical disputes

554
00:29:13,708 --> 00:29:16,665
- or violence against health care workers.
- Hello. Chung Sheng-shan.

555
00:29:16,666 --> 00:29:20,915
As Director of the hospital,
this is the commitment and standard

556
00:29:20,916 --> 00:29:22,875
I owe you all. Thank you.

557
00:29:23,541 --> 00:29:25,957
[Chia-hsin] Thank you
for all your questions.

558
00:29:25,958 --> 00:29:27,457
- Let me see you out.
- Director.

559
00:29:27,458 --> 00:29:30,833
[quietly] I need to talk with you.
Something's happened in the ER.

560
00:29:32,250 --> 00:29:34,000
[indistinct chatter]

561
00:29:37,458 --> 00:29:38,583
Here.

562
00:29:39,125 --> 00:29:40,583
Chou Cheng-chun.

563
00:29:42,125 --> 00:29:43,457
Director.

564
00:29:43,458 --> 00:29:44,707
Dr. Chuang.

565
00:29:44,708 --> 00:29:46,041
Hello, Doctor.

566
00:29:47,041 --> 00:29:50,874
I heard that you just did a thoracotomy.
Did I hear right?

567
00:29:50,875 --> 00:29:53,750
There was a traumatic aortic injury,
so I operated.

568
00:29:54,833 --> 00:29:58,207
You're an Emergency Physician.
Why didn't you wait for a surgeon?

569
00:29:58,208 --> 00:30:00,415
I've had years
of surgical training abroad.

570
00:30:00,416 --> 00:30:03,249
I assessed the patient, he was critical,
he couldn't wait.

571
00:30:03,250 --> 00:30:05,124
The surgeon wasn't ready,
so I made the call.

572
00:30:05,125 --> 00:30:06,665
You still should've waited.

573
00:30:06,666 --> 00:30:10,583
Operating so recklessly puts the patient
at even greater risk

574
00:30:11,208 --> 00:30:13,082
and disregards his rights.

575
00:30:13,083 --> 00:30:14,749
If word gets out

576
00:30:14,750 --> 00:30:18,290
that Yang-Da allowed a doctor
without surgical credentials to operate,

577
00:30:18,291 --> 00:30:19,915
what would the public think?

578
00:30:19,916 --> 00:30:21,749
How would the media report it?

579
00:30:21,750 --> 00:30:23,457
The media is not my concern.

580
00:30:23,458 --> 00:30:26,207
What I care about is not letting
the patient in front of me die.

581
00:30:26,208 --> 00:30:27,291
You--

582
00:30:28,916 --> 00:30:30,041
[Li-te sighs]

583
00:30:31,250 --> 00:30:32,416
Dr. Chou.

584
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,665
How is the patient doing now?

585
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:36,791
Condition's stable. He's recovering well.

586
00:30:37,833 --> 00:30:39,625
Hmm. Great.

587
00:30:40,791 --> 00:30:43,833
I understand
there must be a lot of patients waiting.

588
00:30:44,416 --> 00:30:46,333
It's been a long day for you all.

589
00:30:47,625 --> 00:30:49,250
- Dr. Chung.
- Yes?

590
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:51,957
I'll leave the ER to you.

591
00:30:51,958 --> 00:30:53,125
Yes, sir.

592
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:03,500
[footsteps departing]

593
00:31:10,458 --> 00:31:11,708
[Cheng-chun sighs]

594
00:31:12,500 --> 00:31:13,790
[telephone ringing]

595
00:31:13,791 --> 00:31:17,166
[nurse] Nursing station. Bed 2?
All right, I'll go now.

596
00:31:25,083 --> 00:31:26,957
I know I've never told you this,

597
00:31:26,958 --> 00:31:29,375
but I don't agree
with the anti-violence device.

598
00:31:29,916 --> 00:31:33,082
The maintenance and upkeep alone
are only going to drain the budget

599
00:31:33,083 --> 00:31:35,707
and add to the ER's financial burden.

600
00:31:35,708 --> 00:31:37,374
- [inhales] But--
- Also,

601
00:31:37,375 --> 00:31:41,207
performing surgery in the Resus Room
was an act of pure individualism.

602
00:31:41,208 --> 00:31:43,166
You're lucky that the patient survived.

603
00:31:44,500 --> 00:31:47,208
I'm sure the surgical department
won't be so forgiving.

604
00:31:47,791 --> 00:31:50,166
They'll come at you hard for this.
Good luck.

605
00:31:54,125 --> 00:31:55,290
What's up with him?

606
00:31:55,291 --> 00:31:57,749
So the system is more important
than human lives now?

607
00:31:57,750 --> 00:32:00,290
You saved a patient
from the brink of death.

608
00:32:00,291 --> 00:32:02,208
- Yet you're under review?
- [Cheng-chun sighs]

609
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,375
I support you, man.

610
00:32:04,958 --> 00:32:06,583
All right. Back to work.

611
00:32:10,583 --> 00:32:13,207
[soft classical music playing]

612
00:32:13,208 --> 00:32:15,125
Dad, your medication.

613
00:32:16,666 --> 00:32:17,958
Hey.

614
00:32:18,916 --> 00:32:22,333
It's been such a busy day.
I completely forgot.

615
00:32:23,083 --> 00:32:25,415
- Well, it's not just today.
- [Hsueh-hung sighs]

616
00:32:25,416 --> 00:32:27,791
You performed two surgeries last night.

617
00:32:28,375 --> 00:32:31,041
Dad, it's not for me to say,

618
00:32:31,541 --> 00:32:33,249
but I'm worried about your health.

619
00:32:33,250 --> 00:32:34,958
You're the hospital director.

620
00:32:35,500 --> 00:32:37,666
Why are you still performing surgery?

621
00:32:38,250 --> 00:32:39,832
I appreciate your concern.

622
00:32:39,833 --> 00:32:42,957
But my old patients insist on seeing me.

623
00:32:42,958 --> 00:32:44,833
And I'm worried about them, too.

624
00:32:45,541 --> 00:32:48,750
I know, Dad. You're too sentimental.

625
00:32:49,416 --> 00:32:51,250
Even in the ER just now.

626
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:53,457
You protected Chou Cheng-chun.

627
00:32:53,458 --> 00:32:55,500
Won't there be repercussions?

628
00:32:56,291 --> 00:32:58,665
Are you more concerned about me,

629
00:32:58,666 --> 00:33:00,624
or about Chou Cheng-chun?

630
00:33:00,625 --> 00:33:03,665
[sighs] Just remember
to take your medication.

631
00:33:03,666 --> 00:33:05,583
[Hsueh-hung laughs]

632
00:33:07,583 --> 00:33:09,125
I'll get going.

633
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:16,750
[coffee machine whirring, beeps]

634
00:33:18,666 --> 00:33:20,166
[Cheng-chun] <i>What are you thinking about?</i>

635
00:33:22,666 --> 00:33:24,458
Just the new R1s.

636
00:33:25,208 --> 00:33:28,208
Yeah, I had one of them. Chiang Tung-yen.

637
00:33:28,750 --> 00:33:30,333
He's quite promising.

638
00:33:31,083 --> 00:33:32,415
Mmm-hmm.

639
00:33:32,416 --> 00:33:33,875
How's Lin Geng-ming?

640
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:39,665
I know you fought for his spot here.
An R1 from outside Yang-Da.

641
00:33:39,666 --> 00:33:42,666
I'm not against it. But you know what?

642
00:33:43,333 --> 00:33:45,540
He couldn't even perform an intubation.

643
00:33:45,541 --> 00:33:49,249
[sighs heavily] Yu-hua, I just want
some change around here.

644
00:33:49,250 --> 00:33:51,749
Yeah, you have principles, I know.

645
00:33:51,750 --> 00:33:54,124
Well, I don't like
the current system either.

646
00:33:54,125 --> 00:33:57,291
- But I really don't get why you chose him.
- [Cheng-chun sighs]

647
00:34:07,208 --> 00:34:08,999
[Hsi] What were you busy with earlier?

648
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:10,832
I... just did a REBOA.

649
00:34:10,833 --> 00:34:12,457
- [Tung-yen] Is that so?
- Mmm-hmm.

650
00:34:12,458 --> 00:34:15,666
- I did a thoracotomy with Dr. Chou.
- [Hsi exhales]

651
00:34:18,583 --> 00:34:20,457
[footsteps approaching]

652
00:34:20,458 --> 00:34:22,333
Dr. Chiu. Dr. Huang.

653
00:34:22,833 --> 00:34:25,124
Here, okay? One for each of you.

654
00:34:25,125 --> 00:34:26,415
[amusing music playing]

655
00:34:26,416 --> 00:34:27,750
Where's the other guy?

656
00:34:28,750 --> 00:34:30,874
- I don't know.
- Give it to him later.

657
00:34:30,875 --> 00:34:33,458
- Okay.
- Uh, Doctor, I'm not hungry.

658
00:34:34,208 --> 00:34:37,124
Every R1 has to eat one of these
on their first day in the ER.

659
00:34:37,125 --> 00:34:38,082
It's tradition.

660
00:34:38,083 --> 00:34:41,291
Don't underestimate this humble
red bean bread. [clicks tongue]

661
00:34:42,708 --> 00:34:44,875
- You tell him.
- Come on, aren't we a team?

662
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:49,582
Okay, I'll do it. This item
is from the bake shop downstairs.

663
00:34:49,583 --> 00:34:51,582
But you look straight past it. Why?

664
00:34:51,583 --> 00:34:53,374
- Because it tastes bad.
- Right.

665
00:34:53,375 --> 00:34:56,374
This bad-tasting red bean bread
deserves respect.

666
00:34:56,375 --> 00:34:59,582
When you're working so long and hard
that your vision's blurry,

667
00:34:59,583 --> 00:35:03,083
this is your quickest source of energy
and nothing will taste better.

668
00:35:03,666 --> 00:35:06,082
[sighs] The chaos of the ER.

669
00:35:06,083 --> 00:35:08,832
It's just a tiny part
of the daily routine here.

670
00:35:08,833 --> 00:35:12,416
Your mission now is to survive
until you're an R2, like us.

671
00:35:13,083 --> 00:35:14,666
[whispers] We believe in you.

672
00:35:22,041 --> 00:35:23,790
I'm gonna finish my charts.

673
00:35:23,791 --> 00:35:25,791
Oh, you-- I'm going, too.

674
00:35:38,916 --> 00:35:41,415
[Hsi sighs] We were really busy before.

675
00:35:41,416 --> 00:35:42,875
Where'd you go?

676
00:35:49,333 --> 00:35:51,040
[Geng-ming sighs]

677
00:35:51,041 --> 00:35:52,957
[keyboard clacking]

678
00:35:52,958 --> 00:35:55,415
[Hsiu-ju] Ugh! Finally, a chair.

679
00:35:55,416 --> 00:35:58,415
It's been so busy today.
I forgot what sitting feels like.

680
00:35:58,416 --> 00:36:00,541
Mmm. Mmm.

681
00:36:06,291 --> 00:36:07,666
[exhales]

682
00:36:08,750 --> 00:36:12,000
Is everything okay
with you and Cheng-chun?

683
00:36:13,041 --> 00:36:14,500
Uh, yeah. Why?

684
00:36:15,666 --> 00:36:19,625
No reason. I'm just...
expressing normal concern.

685
00:36:21,083 --> 00:36:23,082
[Yu-hua sighs] Now, tell me.

686
00:36:23,083 --> 00:36:25,040
Are you and Chiu okay?

687
00:36:25,041 --> 00:36:28,166
- Yeah. Um...
- [teasingly] Uh...

688
00:36:28,916 --> 00:36:31,708
I'd be happy if I never saw him again.

689
00:36:32,833 --> 00:36:34,832
[both] Ugh.

690
00:36:34,833 --> 00:36:37,375
Didn't you say
he's the most handsome guy here?

691
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:41,874
[groans] My eyes must have been closed.
Now they're wide open.

692
00:36:41,875 --> 00:36:45,291
So what, your eyes were closed
the whole time you guys were dating?

693
00:36:46,208 --> 00:36:50,375
[sighs] That was three months ago.
The most handsome now is Dr. Chou.

694
00:36:51,083 --> 00:36:54,290
And the second most handsome
is that new one, Tung-yen.

695
00:36:54,291 --> 00:36:57,500
What did you say? Are you even human?

696
00:36:58,083 --> 00:37:00,500
- He's just an R1.
- Uh...

697
00:37:01,041 --> 00:37:04,874
As a senior nurse, I'm only observing
the R1's medical performance.

698
00:37:04,875 --> 00:37:08,249
Ah, yes, senior.
May I ask how the R1s are doing?

699
00:37:08,250 --> 00:37:09,666
Yes, you may.

700
00:37:10,208 --> 00:37:12,458
Well, Tung-yen and Tang Hsi,
they're excellent.

701
00:37:13,041 --> 00:37:15,915
I haven't seen such good R1s in years.

702
00:37:15,916 --> 00:37:19,375
But the other one, Geng-ming?
Well, he's a little strange.

703
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,915
And didn't you give him a talking too?

704
00:37:21,916 --> 00:37:24,832
It turns out he went to Dr. Cheng
to ask him to check on a patient.

705
00:37:24,833 --> 00:37:27,665
Geng-ming spoke up to Dr. Cheng?

706
00:37:27,666 --> 00:37:28,915
Well, yeah.

707
00:37:28,916 --> 00:37:31,832
Dr. Cheng, would you mind
checking on patient Li Wen-hsiung?

708
00:37:31,833 --> 00:37:33,749
- [Wen-hsiung groaning]
<i>- He doesn't look well.</i>

709
00:37:33,750 --> 00:37:35,749
<i>He should be prioritized, right?</i>

710
00:37:35,750 --> 00:37:37,750
- [groaning]
<i>- I think we should get an X-ray.</i>

711
00:37:39,208 --> 00:37:40,708
[Shao-ching smacks lips]

712
00:37:41,375 --> 00:37:44,082
Could you pay a little more attention
to your appearance?

713
00:37:44,083 --> 00:37:45,999
And there's something
you should understand,

714
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,791
R1s don't know it all.

715
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:52,249
He came to pester me about it, too,
asking if you'd check on Wen-hsiung.

716
00:37:52,250 --> 00:37:54,791
You were busy at the time,
so I called Dr. Chou.

717
00:37:55,375 --> 00:37:57,500
Can you believe this kid? [scoffs]

718
00:37:58,125 --> 00:38:01,749
[Yu-hua] "Widening mediastinum
and CP angle blunting."

719
00:38:01,750 --> 00:38:05,375
"Further survey needed. Lin Geng-ming."

720
00:38:07,208 --> 00:38:09,208
[curious music playing]

721
00:38:10,250 --> 00:38:11,165
[music fades]

722
00:38:11,166 --> 00:38:13,416
[water running]

723
00:38:19,333 --> 00:38:21,125
[door opens, closes]

724
00:38:22,416 --> 00:38:24,125
[Chien-te] What did you do to my dad?

725
00:38:27,750 --> 00:38:29,749
Are you Wei Sung's family?

726
00:38:29,750 --> 00:38:31,708
What exactly happened in the ER?

727
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:34,041
[sighs] I...

728
00:38:34,625 --> 00:38:38,291
[shouting] I heard the doctor telling you
to get out of there. So what went wrong?

729
00:38:39,250 --> 00:38:40,957
[Geng-ming breathes shakily]

730
00:38:40,958 --> 00:38:43,832
His mouth was full of blood,
so intubation failed.

731
00:38:43,833 --> 00:38:46,124
But the attending stepped in
and he stabilized--

732
00:38:46,125 --> 00:38:48,915
What do you mean "stabilized"? Huh?

733
00:38:48,916 --> 00:38:50,958
My dad's unconscious right now.

734
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:54,082
If anything happens to him,
I'm coming for you.

735
00:38:54,083 --> 00:38:55,583
So watch your back.

736
00:39:05,708 --> 00:39:08,458
LIN GENG-MING

737
00:39:19,458 --> 00:39:20,915
- [Hsiu-ju grunts]
- [groans]

738
00:39:20,916 --> 00:39:24,124
The tube's in the esophagus.
Get it out now. Suction. Hurry!

739
00:39:24,125 --> 00:39:27,041
What do you mean "stabilized"?
My dad's unconscious right now.

740
00:39:27,625 --> 00:39:30,125
<i>If anything happens to him,
I'm coming for you.</i>

741
00:39:31,875 --> 00:39:34,666
[melancholy music playing]

742
00:39:43,250 --> 00:39:46,166
LIN GENG-MING

743
00:39:51,291 --> 00:39:52,625
[sniffles]

744
00:39:56,125 --> 00:39:58,375
[sighs deeply]

745
00:40:15,083 --> 00:40:17,333
[Cheng-chun] Already defeated
on your first day?

746
00:40:22,375 --> 00:40:23,625
Dr. Chou.

747
00:40:25,791 --> 00:40:27,875
If you can't handle a minor setback,

748
00:40:28,625 --> 00:40:30,499
you should hand in your resignation.

749
00:40:30,500 --> 00:40:32,415
You're not cut out for the emergency ward.

750
00:40:32,416 --> 00:40:34,625
[dramatic music playing]

751
00:40:49,750 --> 00:40:51,791
[music crescendos]

752
00:40:55,041 --> 00:40:57,041
[closing theme music playing]
